       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine, which is 10 mg once daily. The usual adult range is 2.5\u201310 mg. At 50 mg the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, or prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's long half-life of 30\u201350 hours would make that hard to reverse.\n\nThis may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the standard starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for a frail or elderly patient or one with hepatic impairment (not the case for this patient)\n\nIf 50 mg is intentional, please confirm the indication. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
